{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      Fabric.js — Recommended ★\n      \n        Fabric is the library most Canva-like tools are built on. One CDN script\n        gives you: object selection & transforms, rich text editing, image\n        placement, JSON save/load, PNG and SVG export, and a canvas object model\n        that maps directly to your feature list. The UI around it (layers panel,\n        align toolbar, template picker, AI panel) is custom-built to match your\n        existing dark theme.\n      \n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Ships 90% of the hard canvas math already solved\n            JSON serialization = free save/load\n            toDataURL → PNG, toSVG → SVG — one line each\n            380KB CDN, no build step\n            Massive community, tons of patterns for Canva-clones\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            \n              Layers panel, align UI, template picker all need custom code\n            \n            ~380KB added to page weight","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1779570010476}
